                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+principal+bundles"} geometry of physics – principal bundles
              in the section
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "geometry%20of%20physics%20--%20principal%20bundles#PrincipalBundlesViaSmoothGroupoids"} Smooth principal bundles via smooth groupoids
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              of smooth groupoids is presented by a morphism of pre-smooth groupoids after choosing an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              over wich
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              trivialize and choosing a trivialization, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ≃
                                    %mi lwe
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{g_\bullet}{\longrightarrow}&amp; (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq_{lwe}}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
            %p
              where the top morphism is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cocycle
              of the given local trivialization regarded as a morphism out of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+groupoid"} Cech groupoid
              of the given cover.
            %p
              Moreover, by
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+representations+and+associated+bundles#MapFromActionGroupoidOnSetBackToBG"} this proposition
              the morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_\rho)_\bullet
              is a global fibration of pre-smooth groupoids, hence, by the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+homotopy+types"} geometry of physics – smooth homotopy types
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ρ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_\rho)_\bullet
              along this
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_\bullet
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                            %munder
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                                %msub
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi V
                            %mo ⫽
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi V
                            %mo ⫽
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi p
                                    %mi ρ
                                  %msub
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi g
                                  %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                            %msub
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo •
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ≃
                                    %mi lwe
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet \underset{(\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet}{\times} (V \sslash G)_\bullet &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; (V \sslash G)_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{(p_\rho)_\bullet}}
                    \\\
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet &amp;\stackrel{g_\bullet}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    (\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\simeq_{lwe}}}
                    \\\
                    X
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              This pullback is computed componentwise. Hence it is the pre-smooth groupoid whose morphisms are pairs consisting of a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,i)\to (x,j)
              in the Cech groupoid as well as a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \stackrel{g}{\to} \rho(s)(g)
              in the action groupoid, such that the group label
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              of the latter equals the cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_{i j}(x)
              of the cocycle on the former. Schematically:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %munder
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⫽
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo •
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi j
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi s
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C(\{U_i\})_\bullet \underset{(\mathbf{B}G)_\bullet}{\times} (V \sslash G)_\bullet
                    \=
                    \\left\{
                    ((x,i),s) \stackrel{g_{i j}(x)}{\longrightarrow} ((x,j),\rho(s)(g))
                    \\right\}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This means that the pullback groupoid has at most one morphism between every ordered pair of objects. Accordingly this groupoid is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
              equivalent to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of its space of objects by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
              induced by its morphisms:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                      %mo ×
                      %mi V
                      %mo )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{i}{\coprod} U_i \times V
                    \\right)/_\sim
                    \\,.
            %p This is a traditional description of the associated bundle in question.
